126-  compact={compact}
127-  menuDensity="compact"
128-  menuItems={menuItems}
129-  onChangeCompact={setCompact}
130-/>
131-```
132-
133-The default value is `default`, which preserves the previous dimensions. Compact density reduces
134-menu, subheader, and footer item icons; it does not resize the standard 24 px logo icon.
135-With the advanced layout pattern, pass `menuDensity` to `PageLayout`; `PageLayoutAside` inherits
136-the normalized value from context.
137-
138-### Top decoration
139-
140-Navigation highlights top section with Logo and Subheader items using `headerDecoration` props.
141-
142-### Section dividers
143-
144-`hideSectionDividers` hides the header/footer separators (including the collapsed header decoration SVG) and their spacing toward the menu. Header background, outer spacing, and separators inside the menu/Quick Access are preserved.
145-
146-With `hideSectionDividers=true`, indicators appear at the menu scroll edges only while content is hidden beyond that edge: bottom at the start, both in the middle, top at the end, neither without overflow. They do not restore spacing. With `false`, the existing footer separator remains visible whenever the menu overflows, including at the end. The Quick Access separator stays inside the scrolling content and can coexist with these indicators. Setting `--gn-aside-header-divider-horizontal-color: transparent` also hides the scroll indicators.
147-
148-The property is supported by `AsideHeader` and `PageLayoutAside`. `AsideFallback` supports hiding separators and spacing only: it has no scrollable menu and does not render scroll-edge indicators.
149-
150-### Custom background
151-
152:The component supports specific themization cases, e.g. image on background or splitting sections by color — using `customBackground`, `customBackgroundClassName` props.
153-
154-## Sections
155-
156-Navigation includes 3 parts: the top, the middle and the bottom. These sections are similar with a few variations of possibilities based on frequency user cases.
157-**Important note**: A user manages the state of the elements.
158-
159-### The Top
160-
161-The section usually contains general elements for all site pages and includes the logo and the elements below it. Clickable logo can be useful for a quick navigation to the home page, if necessary the element (e.g. search, catalogue) is placed under it.
162-
163-### The Middle (menuItems)
164-
165-The main section usually depends on context of the page — one of examples using navigation on the multipage sites.
166-The elements will collapse into three dots if there is no vertical space by default.
167-
168-Navigation elements can be in one of two states: collapsed (isCollapsed), where only the icon is visible, and expanded. There is some space for customization of the entire item through a wrapper.
169-
170-With additional configuration via `AllPages` users can further customize menu to their preference by hiding unnecessary items. This brings in a new state for items - `hidden`. If item is pinned, it will always be displayed in the section.
171-
172-The `onMenuItemsChanged` callback is required for adding extra component `All Pages` which displays panel for editing the list of visible menu items.
173-
174-While the built-in **All pages** panel is open, its menu row is the only one highlighted as
175-current: current highlights of consumer menu items, group header rows, and quick access rows are
176-visually muted and restored as soon as the panel closes. Item data is not modified — `current`
177-flags stay intact in `menuItems` and in the panel itself.
178-
179-**Important note**: A user manages a modified list of the menu items that they receive from the callback and provides the new state of items to `AsideHeader`.
180-
181-The elements of this block can have multiple tooltips.
182-
183-#### Quick access
184-
185-Set `enableQuickAccess` to render menu items marked with `quickAccess: true` in a separate section
186-and to expose pin controls for eligible leaf items. Quick access is controlled: the component never
187-mutates `menuItems`; update the item in `onQuickAccessChange` and pass the resulting array back.
188-Without `onQuickAccessChange`, marked items remain visible as a read-only section and pin controls
189-are hidden.
